<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uncas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1588–c. 1683</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uncas was a sachem of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohegan">Mohegan</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a>. A Pequot noble by birth, he broke away from the Pequot leadership in the 1630s and allied with the English, fighting beside them in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pequot-war">Pequot War</a> of 1637. Supported by the colonists, he made the Mohegan the leading native power of the region and in 1643 captured and had killed his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narragansett-people">Narragansett</a> rival Miantonomoh.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uncas.jpg" alt="Uncas" width="320" height="485" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edmund Ollier · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Uncas_and_Miantonomoh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
